---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Services — LinksMaxing"
  description="Nine signals across three surfaces. Correlated in real time. A prioritized decision list — what to build, what to fix, what to publish, in what order."
  activeNav="services"
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="page-eyebrow">Services</div>
    <h1 class="page-title">Nine signals. Seven <em>decisions.</em></h1>
    <p class="page-lead">We correlate the data other agencies can't produce, then ship the work the data points to. Every page for a reason. Every number traced back to the signal that moved.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="block block-grid">
    <div class="block-meta">
      <div class="block-meta-num">01</div>
      <div class="block-meta-cat">Signals</div>
      <div class="block-meta-items">
        <div class="block-meta-item"><strong>9</strong> signals</div>
        <div class="block-meta-item"><strong>3</strong> surfaces</div>
        <div class="block-meta-item">Correlated in real time</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2 class="sec-head">What we <em>watch.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-beat">Everyone else watches one signal. Maybe two. <em>Nine is where correlation lives.</em></p>

      <div class="article-body" style="border-top:none;padding-top:0;max-width:100%;">
        <h3>Assistants</h3>
        <p><strong>AI recommendations —</strong> Every query your customer might ask, run against ChatGPT, Claude, and Google AI Overviews. Who names you. Who names competitors. Who names nobody.</p>
        <p><strong>Source retrieval —</strong> Which pages each assistant actually reads to build its answer. The source graph nobody else maps.</p>
        <p><strong>Competitor entities —</strong> Which categories, licenses, credentials, and citations your competitors claim that you don't.</p>

        <h3>Search</h3>
        <p><strong>Google Search Console —</strong> What queries actually drive impressions today. What ranks. What clicks. The gap between what customers ask and what your site answers.</p>
        <p><strong>Technical SEO —</strong> Core Web Vitals, JavaScript rendering, sitemap health, canonical hygiene, robots access per crawler.</p>
        <p><strong>Content gaps —</strong> Questions your customers ask that your site doesn't yet answer. The prescriptive side of GSC.</p>

        <h3>Ground truth</h3>
        <p><strong>Site structure —</strong> Whether crawlers can even reach what you publish. Schema validity. NAP consistency. Heading hierarchy.</p>
        <p><strong>Google Business Profile —</strong> Categories, photos, review response, posts, hours accuracy. The signals Google feeds back to itself.</p>
        <p><strong>Reviews —</strong> Sentiment, volume, response cadence, and — critically — what phrases customers use that AI can re-quote.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="pull-quote">Nine signals. Correlated. One <em>decision list.</em></div>

  <section class="block block-grid">
    <div class="block-meta">
      <div class="block-meta-num">02</div>
      <div class="block-meta-cat">Decisions</div>
      <div class="block-meta-items">
        <div class="block-meta-item"><strong>7</strong> ship types</div>
        <div class="block-meta-item">Every fix attributed</div>
        <div class="block-meta-item">No hunches</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2 class="sec-head">What we <em>ship.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-beat">No page ships on instinct. <em>No fix on hunch.</em></p>

      <div class="article-body" style="border-top:none;padding-top:0;max-width:100%;">
        <p><strong>Site rebuild —</strong> Crawler-native architecture on Astro. Server-rendered, zero-JS by default, structured for retrieval. When the site itself is blocking the work, this is the first ship.</p>
        <p><strong>Answer pages —</strong> Every query your customers ask, given a page shaped as an answer. Retrievable by name.</p>
        <p><strong>Entity graph —</strong> Schema, categories, credentials, service areas. Claimed and structured so assistants understand what you are.</p>
        <p><strong>Evidence pages —</strong> Case studies, reviews, credentials, dated observations. What the assistants cite when they name you.</p>
        <p><strong>GBP management —</strong> Posts, review response, category and photo hygiene. Weekly cadence, tracked against the scan.</p>
        <p><strong>Technical fixes —</strong> Schema, JSON-LD, sitemap, crawler access. The blocker list that makes everything else possible.</p>
        <p><strong>Measurement —</strong> Baseline before we ship. Cadence scans after. Delta reports tied back to the signal that moved.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="pull-quote">Every ship carries the <em>signal</em> that scoped it.</div>

  <section class="block block-grid">
    <div class="block-meta">
      <div class="block-meta-num">03</div>
      <div class="block-meta-cat">Engagement</div>
      <div class="block-meta-items">
        <div class="block-meta-item"><strong>3</strong> ways to work</div>
        <div class="block-meta-item">Fixed scope</div>
        <div class="block-meta-item">Cancel anytime</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="block-body">
      <h2 class="sec-head">Three ways to <em>work with us.</em></h2>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="grid-3-cell">
          <div class="grid-3-label">Start here</div>
          <div class="grid-3-name">Visibility check</div>
          <div class="grid-3-desc">One-time scan and correlation report. Roughly a week. Fixed scope, fixed price. <a href="/scan" style="color:var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--oxblood);text-decoration:none;">Details →</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-3-cell">
          <div class="grid-3-label">Bigger work</div>
          <div class="grid-3-name">Project</div>
          <div class="grid-3-desc">A rebuild, a schema overhaul, a set of answer pages, a GBP cleanup. Scoped from the visibility check. Fixed timeline, one deliverable.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-3-cell">
          <div class="grid-3-label">Ongoing</div>
          <div class="grid-3-name">Retainer</div>
          <div class="grid-3-desc">Monthly scans and cadence work. Month-to-month, cancel anytime. Every deliverable tied to a signal that moved.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-block">
    <h2 class="cta-head">Start with a <em>scan.</em></h2>
    <p class="cta-sub">Everything else follows from the data. Twenty minutes on a call, three to five days to run the scan, then a real conversation about what the data says.</p>
    <a href="/scan" class="btn">Book a visibility check →</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
